Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 15:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] iOS: cloud saves through the Dropbox API, with the status beside Play

A local patch, not for upstream. Dropbox's folder in the Files app can hand
back an old copy of a file changed on another device, so a game can start
with an old save and believe it is in step. With Documents/dropbox.txt in
place the app reads and writes save.dmsync on Dropbox's servers itself; the
same file stays visible in the folder, and save_sync.c still decides.

The launcher asks Dropbox before Play and shows the result beside the
button. Play asks once more; when the save cannot be read, the game does not
start until the player answers Continue: Yes or No.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
